      "postID": "62eec7467421b444aeafbcac",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5d6ac3d319a45a329c545086|full_name}: People not understanding how to do basic debugging steps should not be a reason for me to lack a useful feature.\n\nAt the very least, we should be able to persist the dynamic mode in the config file. I would imagine that if I have visual artifacts in a world, I would know to change it away from dynamic.\n\nEvery time I play the game, I usually turn on the near clip when I join, or I turn it on when I noticed I need it. I then proceed to play for another 2-8+ hours straight hopping between worlds and never having an issue with dynamic clipping.\n\nThere's only one or two worlds of the couple hundred I've visited recently that have had an issue with it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
